    "body": "## Problem\n\nA language server may return a `textDocument/documentLink` result with\nno `target`, deferring resolution to a `documentLink/resolve`\nround-trip — the same lazy-resolution pattern already used for\n`codeLens/resolve` and `completionItem/resolve`. The `vim.ui.open()`/\n`gx` consumer of document links (`get_lsp_urls()` in `vim/ui.lua`) only\never read the link's `target` eagerly and silently dropped any link\nthat omitted one, since nothing anywhere resolved it.\n\n## Solution\n\nCall `documentLink/resolve` synchronously (mirroring the synchronous\n`textDocument/documentLink` request this function already makes) when\na link has no `target` and the client advertises `resolveProvider`,\nand use the resolved target in its place.\n\nPart of #37691 (adds the `documentLink/resolve` item; leaves the\nseparate extmark-tracking idea in that issue untouched).",
